title: End of the Civil War
subtitle: Victory at last!!!
on-arrival: civil_war = 0; army_strength = 50;
tags: event
view-if: year = 1865 and month = 4
face-image: img/General_Robert_E._Lee_surrenders_at_Appomattox_Court_House_1865.jpg
max-visits: 1
 
The long and bloody conflict draws to a close. General Robert E. Lee, commanding the battered remnants of the Confederate Army of Northern Virginia, has surrendered to Union General Ulysses S. Grant. The terms are generous—officers may keep their swords, men their horses.

The guns fall silent. After four years, the Civil War is effectively over.
